    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is lower triangular: **true**. All entries above the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $-2\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}-A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $-2\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
